      "content": "Labor unions were a vital force in strengthening American democracy by directly challenging the unchecked power of industrial capitalism. They achieved this by organizing workers to demand fair wages and safe conditions, effectively giving the working class a collective voice in economic decisions. This collective bargaining power forced corporations to acknowledge the rights of the individual worker, which is a fundamental pillar of a healthy democracy. Ultimately, unions democratized the workplace, making the system more equitable and representative of the populace.",
